title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Use the keyboard only
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Everything on the canvas can be done without a mouse: steps and the list are focusable, Enter opens the editor, arrow keys move a step, Delete removes it, and the settings have a menu for connecting steps. Changes are announced to screen readers, and colour is never the only signal.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Tab into the page"
click c1 "Tab to a group in the 'Steps' list and press Enter to open it"
click c2 "Tab to a step in the list and press Enter"
process p1 "The step is added in the free place nearest the middle of the view and selected\nAnnounced: 'Added Create task'"
click c3 "Tab to the canvas and on to a step (each step is a focusable group)\nPress Enter"
process p2 "The step is selected and the focus moves to the heading of its settings"
click c4 "Press the arrow keys on a selected step"
process p3 "The step moves 20 px per press (Shift: 80), snapped to the grid\nA run of presses is one undo step"
click c5 "In the settings, under 'Next steps', pick where each exit leads\n(a list of the steps that can be connected)"
process p4 "The line is drawn, or removed when 'Not connected' is chosen\nAnnounced: 'Connected Start to Create task'"
click c6 "Press Delete on a selected step"
process p5 "The step and its lines go\nAnnounced: 'Deleted'"
click c7 "Press Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z or Ctrl+S"
process p6 "Undone, redone, or the draft is saved\nAnnounced: 'Undone', 'Redone', 'Draft saved'"
click c8 "Press Escape"
process p7 "Closes the pop-up, menu or panel on top, one at a time"
screen sr "For people who cannot see colour\nStatus is words and shapes: 'Live', 'Demo simulation', 'Not configured' dots differ in shape,\nrun states say Done, Skipped, Failed, Waiting, Pending, Not reached\nValidation marks have a name: 'Needs fixing' or 'Check'"
end e1 "A workflow was built, connected and edited with the keyboard"

s1 --> c1 --> c2 --> p1 --> c3 --> p2
p2 --> c4 --> p3
p2 --> c5 --> p4
p2 --> c6 --> p5
p3 --> c7
p4 --> c7
p5 --> c7 --> p6 --> c8 --> p7 --> e1
p2 --> sr
